    <title>Engineering Lead</title>
    <link>http://localhost:1313/roles/engineering-lead-3f16e8cb553e80c8b4f8ceb5851b8458/</link>
    <pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 00:52:00 &#43;0000</pubDate><author>
        <name>Author</name>
    </author><guid>http://localhost:1313/roles/engineering-lead-3f16e8cb553e80c8b4f8ceb5851b8458/</guid>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2 id="duties--responsibilities" class="headerLink">
    <a href="#duties--responsibilities" class="header-mark"></a>Duties &amp; Responsibilities</h2><ul>
<li>Lead the research and development across all of BiOM’s engineering sub-teams and manage the technical efforts made towards conservation projects.</li>
<li>Make/escalate purchase requests, complaints, suggestions, and unresolved problems with senior BiOM leadership.</li>
<li>Collect and organise various resources and documents to ensure seamless leadership transition.</li>
<li>Connect and engage with internal and external stakeholders including academic advisors.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-were-looking-for" class="headerLink">
    <a href="#what-were-looking-for" class="header-mark"></a>What we’re looking for</h2><ul>
<li>Familiarity with BiOM values, vision, and mission.</li>
<li>An aptitude to lead and/or real experience leading a range of teams or projects: planning timelines, supporting members, allocating resources and resolving interpersonal conflicts.</li>
<li>Reliable and consistent communications between leadership and sub-team members.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
